  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Critical temperature is :-</p><p><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>27</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br />for <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> the value of <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> is the highest so,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></msub></math> for <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> will be highest.<br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> for <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3.2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0.406</mn></math><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> for <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1.7</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0.118</mn></math><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> for <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5.1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5.1</mn></math><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> for <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4.1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0.82</mn></math></p>"
